	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/mods_settings/help_strings">
		<string text="Texture, sound, text and model packs from the mods folder, and the Theater's recorded games."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Texture, sound, text and model packs from the mods folder: turn each on or off, and choose which plays over which. They are this computer's, for every profile."/>
		<string text="Each mod is a folder in the mods folder, beside the maps folder, with its mod.toml and its tags. Mods are turned on and off from the main menu's Settings, not in a game."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Records each network game you play or host, from the next one on, to watch again in the Theater."/>
		<string text="The games recorded: watch one again from any player's view, or a free or cinematic camera."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Gives weapons and armour the fine grain of their surfaces (machining, weave, wear) from a mod's material overlay. It changes only the light on them. Off draws them as the Xbox did."/>
		<string text="Draws the sharper textures mods ship in place of the game's, once they are in the graphics card's memory. Stock draws the game's own."/>
		<string text="How much of the graphics card's memory mods' textures may take. Auto takes six tenths of what is free; past it, those not seen lately go back to the game's."/>
		<string text="Lights armour and weapons with the materials mods give them: their colour, bumps, roughness, metal and coats under the level's own lights. Stock draws them as the Xbox did."/>
		<string text="On graphics cards that trace rays: Shadows casts the sun's shadows of everything on screen and traced ambient occlusion; GI also bounces the light of plasma, muzzle flashes and the sky about the characters. The level keeps its own brightness and colours. Off draws the game's own light."/>
		<string text="More rays a pixel: softer, steadier shadows and more of the bounced light, at more of the graphics card's time. Low suits the Steam Deck."/>
	</strings>
